From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:52:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: read every clone argument its flags use

linux-wasm's variadic __clone read tls and ctid only under
CLONE_CHILD_SETTID. pthread_create passes CLONE_SETTLS |
CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID without it, so every thread started with a TLS
pointer of 0 (pthread_self() returned 0) and no clear-tid address, so
pthread_join was never woken and the last worker to exit ended the
process with status 0. The arguments come in order, so each one a flag
uses is read; posix_spawn, which passes none, sets none of those flags.
---
diff --git a/src/linux/clone.c b/src/linux/clone.c
index e3e8aa0..4ee14b2 100644
--- a/src/linux/clone.c
+++ b/src/linux/clone.c
@@ -71,10 +71,12 @@ int __clone(int (*fn)(void *), void *stack, int flags, void *arg, ...)
 	pid_t *ptid = 0, *ctid = 0;
 	void  *tls = 0;
 
+	/* gmux: the variadic arguments come in order, so each one a flag uses must be read, and
+	 * pthread_create passes CLONE_SETTLS | CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID without CLONE_CHILD_SETTID */
 	va_start(ap, arg);
-	if (flags & (CLONE_PIDFD | CLONE_PARENT_SETTID | CLONE_CHILD_SETTID))
+	if (flags & (CLONE_PIDFD | CLONE_PARENT_SETTID | CLONE_SETTLS | CLONE_CHILD_SETTID | CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID))
 		ptid = va_arg(ap, pid_t *);
-	if (flags & CLONE_CHILD_SETTID) {
+	if (flags & (CLONE_SETTLS | CLONE_CHILD_SETTID | CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID)) {
 		tls = va_arg(ap, void *);
 		ctid = va_arg(ap, pid_t *);
 	}
